msgid ""
"<p>The so-called <b>Ping</b> is an ICMP packet that is sent to a host to check "
"if it's running or not."
"<br>\n"
"If you disable \"Reply to echo-request\", your computer will be invisible for "
"most of the common programs used to hack/crack hosts on the Internet."
"<br>\n"
"However, there are a lot of network programs that use ping requests to find and "
"check the connections to their client/server host.</p>"
